Here is the patch, for 3.1.0.  However, you cannot go on the high score list
if you enter discovery mode.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you've ever wished that you could keep playing your game after getting
killed, here's the patch for you.  Insert it about 400 lines down in
src/end.c, and recompile.

(400 lines is just an estimate.  The patch is between the lines of hyphens.
The stuff before the first line of hyphens and after the 2nd line of hyphens
is just there to show you *exactly* where to place it in end.c.  Search
through the file for the phrase "Do not pass go" and you should end up in
the right place.)

If you have any trouble with it, let me know.  You could, of course, remove
the line that says "discover=1", effectively being both immortal *and* eligible
for the high score list, but I don't advocate doing that.  (You'd just have
to say "yes" twice each time you died, and you'd be back at full hit points,
in perfect condition again.)

This is, of course, *NOT* an official patch.  The dev team will probably be
sending a hit man after me any time now  :-)

I'm working on a slightly more useful one, that will allow you to be placed
on the high score list before entering Discover mode, but that will be a while
yet.

--Robert DeLoura
deloura@noaapmel.gov

###############################################################################

	if (moves <= 1 && how < QUIT)
	    /* You die... --More-- */
	    pline("Do not pass go.  Do not collect 200 zorkmids.");
/*---------------------------------------------------------------------*/
/* Code added to allow you to enter Discovery Mode when you die.  -RAD */
#if defined(EXPLORE_MODE)
	if((how != QUIT) && (yn("Enter discovery mode?")=='y')) {
		pline("You will invalidate your score if you proceed.");
		if(yn("Are you sure you want to enter discovery mode?")=='y') {
			discover = TRUE;
			You("are now in discovery mode.");
			You("feel much better.");
			savelife(QUIT);
			killer = 0;
			return;
		}
	}
#endif		
/*---------------------------------------------------------------------*/
die:
	if (have_windows) wait_synch();	/* flush screen output */





